# Token Registry Validation

This rule defines how token references must be validated against `docs/_generated/token-registry.json`.

## Blocking checks

- Every token path referenced in docs/specs must resolve in `docs/_generated/token-registry.json`.
- Token paths are case-sensitive and should match canonical registry keys exactly.
- Dot and slash aliases must resolve deterministically to the same canonical entry.

## Error codes

Internal governance codes emitted by the validator:

| Code | Source | Meaning |
| ---- | ------ | ------- |
| `TOK01` | Markdown prose | Token path not found in registry |
| `TOK02` | Markdown prose | Token path deprecated |
| `TOK03` | Markdown prose | Forbidden `VariableID:*` format |
| `SPEC01` | Spec YAML `token_mapping` | Token path not found in registry |

The standalone token-ref report (see below) maps these to four buckets:
`unresolved_tokens`, `wrong_format_tokens`, `case_mismatch_tokens`, `deprecated_tokens`.

## Validation commands

**Focused token-reference report** (preferred for CI and pre-promote checks):

```bash
npm run validate:token-refs
```

Options:
```bash
npm run validate:token-refs -- --component-name Alert      # single component
npm run validate:token-refs -- --spec-file docs/_spec/components/alert.yml
npm run validate:token-refs -- --file docs/components/alert.md
npm run validate:token-refs -- --json                      # machine-readable JSON
npm run validate:token-refs -- --no-specs                  # skip spec YAML files
npm run validate:token-refs -- --no-markdown               # skip markdown files
```

Exit codes: `0` clean · `1` unresolved tokens · `2` wrong-format tokens · `3` both.

**Full docs validation** (structural + token + all other rules):

```bash
npm run validate:docs
```
